  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...An upper ridge centered over the Southeast CONUS\nand sfc high pressure ridging in from the north will keep dry\nconditions across ENC through much of the work week. However,  \nupper low retrograding to the SSW across the offshore waters \nThursday into Friday may bring a few showers near the Gulf\nStream, but dry conditions expected to persist across land \nareas. Gusty NEerly winds will continue until around sunset\nwhen they will begin to ease. NE flow regime remains in place \nthrough mid week bringing seasonable temperatures and \ncomfortable humidity levels, then will see gradually warming \nand increasing dewpoints Thursday into Friday as high pressure \nweakens and slides offshore allowing low level flow to veer to \nsoutherly ahead of an approaching cold front. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A weak cold front will drop south into the area\nSaturday and briefly stall before lifting back north as a cold\nfront on Sunday. Sfc convergence and lowering heights aloft as \nshortwave energy rides over the upper ridge along with\nincreasing moisture will allow for a better chance of showers \nand thunderstorms across the area over the weekend and into \nearly next week, especially through peak heating when \ninstability is greatest.",
